NOTICE
======

This repository is a collection of computer-vision research code written at
Kesowa between 2021 and 2025. It is published for reference. The notes below
record what we know about the provenance of the code and the model weights, so
that anyone reusing them can check their own obligations.

Source code
-----------

The Python source in this repository was written by Kesowa and is MIT licensed,
with the exception of code that is clearly adapted from an upstream project.
Where that is the case, the file says so.

A copy of YOLOv7's `detect.py` (GPL-3.0, github.com/WongKinYiu/yolov7) was
previously present under `construction_material/`. It has been removed, because
GPL-3.0 code cannot be redistributed under this repository's MIT licence. If you
need that script, take it from upstream under its own terms.

Model weights
-------------

Trained weights are distributed here as a convenience and are NOT covered by
the MIT licence. Each derives from an upstream pretrained model, and the
upstream terms continue to apply:

  Face_recognition/           VGG-Face architecture. The original VGG-Face
                              weights from the University of Oxford are released
                              for non-commercial research use only. Treat
                              anything derived from them accordingly.

  Tree_detection/             DeepForest (MIT), itself pretrained on NEON
  Tree Count/                 airborne data. Check NEON's data policy for
                              derived-product obligations.

  Roof_top_segmentation/      U-Net trained on Kesowa imagery. The architecture
                              is generic; the training data was ours.

  construction_material/      Fine-tuned from YOLOv7, which is GPL-3.0. Weights
                              fine-tuned from a GPL model occupy contested legal
                              ground. Seek advice before commercial use.

  Violence_detection/         Keras model. Upstream pretraining lineage is not
                              recorded; provenance unverified.

  people_count/               Expects YOLOv3 / YOLOv4-tiny weights, which are
                              not distributed here. Obtain them from upstream.

Where a lineage is marked unverified, we genuinely do not know. Do not read
silence as permission.

Personal data
-------------

An earlier version of this repository contained facial photographs of
identifiable individuals under `Face_recognition/`, committed in 2021 as sample
data. Those images, the accompanying video and a label encoder mapping
embeddings to names were removed from the entire git history in 2026, and the
history was rewritten. No facial images of identifiable people remain in this
repository.

The face-recognition source code remains. It ships with no dataset; you must
supply your own, and you are responsible for having a lawful basis to process
whatever images you use. Facial images are sensitive personal data under the
Indian DPDP Act 2023 and the EU GDPR, among others.

Geospatial references
---------------------

Some scripts contain coordinates and endpoint URLs from Kesowa survey projects,
left in as examples. They refer to internal infrastructure that is not publicly
reachable. They are not credentials.
